{"id": "EUVD-2026-103844", "enisaUuid": "64bd0d1b-eddf-3a20-b60d-4e2e8672a6e8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: tipd: fix uninitialized typec_partner_desc in cd321x_update_work()\n\ncd321x_update_work() passes a stack-allocated typec_partner_desc to\ntypec_register_partner() after initializing only usb_pd, accessory and\nidentity.\n\ntypec_register_partner() copies attach and deattach from the descriptor\ninto the partner. With those fields left unset, garbage function pointers\nmay be stored and later invoked from typec_partner_link_device() when a USB\ndevice is linked to the port. Uninitialized pd_revision and usb_capability\nsimilarly leak stack data through partner sysfs.\n\nZero-initialize the descriptor so optional callbacks remain NULL and the\nremaining fields are zero.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:25:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75dc6cb377efd2f4428b7f76d3a590a0bbc10399", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5414144e202a32437e3eb436cd3f5f00d79ad86e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88c7e458af53ff781a3f1051708395892b325576"], "aliases": ["GHSA-34hh-4678-7488", "CVE-2026-98759"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "27241fa6-22c1-3a19-aaca-5e35d7531676", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "660f4768-85ff-3872-b5c6-0381bec834d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82432bbfb9e83b7e81d04660fe129b99a29b2ac2 <5414144e202a32437e3eb436cd3f5f00d79ad86e"}, {"id": "6a0992ac-7ceb-31f2-b599-21e688eeccc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7224f48a-fd1d-3de5-8d25-ef03752e0687", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "754279fb-23b2-3223-93a8-4c6a67c6b4c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "84f92471-ffea-3650-919b-d3a7a336623c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82432bbfb9e83b7e81d04660fe129b99a29b2ac2 <88c7e458af53ff781a3f1051708395892b325576"}, {"id": "8ec29222-34b7-34ae-8b89-ec9116a512a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "d1638eb1-885b-3c09-b17f-ba0eef88dd05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82432bbfb9e83b7e81d04660fe129b99a29b2ac2 <75dc6cb377efd2f4428b7f76d3a590a0bbc10399"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "13ded4bf-b342-387c-ba8c-7a88176b72b6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}